{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"docker-tools","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Docker Tools","description":"The everyday Docker and Docker Compose commands from the command palette. Dangerous ones ask first.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:dockerTools.menu","onCommand:dockerTools.dockerfileBuild","onCommand:dockerTools.ps","onCommand:dockerTools.psAll","onCommand:dockerTools.images","onCommand:dockerTools.volumes","onCommand:dockerTools.networks","onCommand:dockerTools.stats","onCommand:dockerTools.logs","onCommand:dockerTools.shell","onCommand:dockerTools.inspect","onCommand:dockerTools.start","onCommand:dockerTools.stop","onCommand:dockerTools.restart","onCommand:dockerTools.rm","onCommand:dockerTools.pull","onCommand:dockerTools.build","onCommand:dockerTools.run","onCommand:dockerTools.composeUp","onCommand:dockerTools.composeUpBuild","onCommand:dockerTools.composeDown","onCommand:dockerTools.composeStop","onCommand:dockerTools.composeRestart","onCommand:dockerTools.composePs","onCommand:dockerTools.composeLogs","onCommand:dockerTools.composeLogsOne","onCommand:dockerTools.composeExec","onCommand:dockerTools.composeBuild","onCommand:dockerTools.composePull","onCommand:dockerTools.composeConfig","onCommand:dockerTools.composeDownVolumes","onCommand:dockerTools.prune"],"permissions":["terminal"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"dockerTools.menu","title":"Docker Menu...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.dockerfileBuild","title":"Build the Open Dockerfile...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.ps","title":"Show Running Containers","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.psAll","title":"Show All Containers","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.images","title":"Show Images","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.volumes","title":"Show Volumes","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.networks","title":"Show Networks","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.stats","title":"Show Resource Use","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.logs","title":"Follow Logs of a Container...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.shell","title":"Open a Shell in a Container...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.inspect","title":"Inspect a Container...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.start","title":"Start a Container...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.stop","title":"Stop a Container...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.restart","title":"Restart a Container...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.rm","title":"Remove a Container...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.pull","title":"Pull an Image...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.build","title":"Build an Image from This Folder...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.run","title":"Run an Image...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeUp","title":"Compose: Start Services in the Background","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeUpBuild","title":"Compose: Rebuild and Start","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeDown","title":"Compose: Stop and Remove Services","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeStop","title":"Compose: Stop Services","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeRestart","title":"Compose: Restart Services","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composePs","title":"Compose: Show Services","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeLogs","title":"Compose: Follow Logs","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeLogsOne","title":"Compose: Follow Logs of a Service...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeExec","title":"Compose: Open a Shell in a Service...","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeBuild","title":"Compose: Build Images","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composePull","title":"Compose: Pull Images","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeConfig","title":"Compose: Check and Show the Final Config","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.composeDownVolumes","title":"Compose: Stop and Delete Services and Volumes","category":"Docker Tools"},{"command":"dockerTools.prune","title":"Clean Up Unused Docker Data","category":"Docker Tools"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"dockerTools.menu","key":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+D"}],"configuration":{"title":"Docker Tools","properties":{"dockerTools.composeCommand":{"type":"string","default":"docker compose","description":"The Compose command: \"docker compose\" (Compose v2) or \"docker-compose\" (v1)."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Docker Tools: the everyday Docker and Docker Compose commands from the command palette. Each one types the command in the terminal,\n// where you can see it run. Commands that delete things ask first.\n\n/** A container, image, service or volume name that is safe to put in a command. */\nconst SAFE = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_.:/@-]{0,200}$/;\nconst safeName = (s) => (SAFE.test(String(s || '').trim()) ? String(s).trim() : null);\n\n/** The list of actions: id, title, command template, optional prompt for one argument, optional confirmation. */\nfunction actions(compose) {\n  return [\n    { id: 'ps', title: 'Show Running Containers', cmd: 'docker ps' },\n    { id: 'psAll', title: 'Show All Containers', cmd: 'docker ps -a' },\n    { id: 'images', title: 'Show Images', cmd: 'docker images' },\n    { id: 'volumes', title: 'Show Volumes', cmd: 'docker volume ls' },\n    { id: 'networks', title: 'Show Networks', cmd: 'docker network ls' },\n    { id: 'stats', title: 'Show Resource Use', cmd: 'docker stats --no-stream' },\n    { id: 'logs', title: 'Follow Logs of a Container...', cmd: 'docker logs -f --tail 200 {name}', ask: 'container' },\n    { id: 'shell', title: 'Open a Shell in a Container...', cmd: 'docker exec -it {name} sh', ask: 'container' },\n    { id: 'inspect', title: 'Inspect a Container...', cmd: 'docker inspect {name}', ask: 'container' },\n    { id: 'start', title: 'Start a Container...', cmd: 'docker start {name}', ask: 'container' },\n    { id: 'stop', title: 'Stop a Container...', cmd: 'docker stop {name}', ask: 'container' },\n    { id: 'restart', title: 'Restart a Container...', cmd: 'docker restart {name}', ask: 'container' },\n    { id: 'rm', title: 'Remove a Container...', cmd: 'docker rm {name}', ask: 'container', confirm: 'Remove the container {name}?' },\n    { id: 'pull', title: 'Pull an Image...', cmd: 'docker pull {name}', ask: 'image' },\n    { id: 'build', title: 'Build an Image from This Folder...', cmd: 'docker build -t {name} .', ask: 'tag for the image (name:tag)' },\n    { id: 'run', title: 'Run an Image...', cmd: 'docker run --rm -it {name}', ask: 'image' },\n    { id: 'composeUp', title: 'Compose: Start Services in the Background', cmd: compose + ' up -d' },\n    { id: 'composeUpBuild', title: 'Compose: Rebuild and Start', cmd: compose + ' up -d --build' },\n    { id: 'composeDown', title: 'Compose: Stop and Remove Services', cmd: compose + ' down' },\n    { id: 'composeStop', title: 'Compose: Stop Services', cmd: compose + ' stop' },\n    { id: 'composeRestart', title: 'Compose: Restart Services', cmd: compose + ' restart' },\n    { id: 'composePs', title: 'Compose: Show Services', cmd: compose + ' ps' },\n    { id: 'composeLogs', title: 'Compose: Follow Logs', cmd: compose + ' logs -f --tail 200' },\n    { id: 'composeLogsOne', title: 'Compose: Follow Logs of a Service...', cmd: compose + ' logs -f --tail 200 {name}', ask: 'service' },\n    { id: 'composeExec', title: 'Compose: Open a Shell in a Service...', cmd: compose + ' exec {name} sh', ask: 'service' },\n    { id: 'composeBuild', title: 'Compose: Build Images', cmd: compose + ' build' },\n    { id: 'composePull', title: 'Compose: Pull Images', cmd: compose + ' pull' },\n    { id: 'composeConfig', title: 'Compose: Check and Show the Final Config', cmd: compose + ' config' },\n    { id: 'composeDownVolumes', title: 'Compose: Stop and Delete Services and Volumes', cmd: compose + ' down -v', confirm: 'This deletes the containers AND their volumes (database data). Continue?' },\n    { id: 'prune', title: 'Clean Up Unused Docker Data', cmd: 'docker system prune', confirm: 'Remove stopped containers, unused networks and dangling images?' },\n  ];\n}\n\n/** Fills the template. Returns null when the name is not safe. */\nfunction build(action, name) {\n  if (!action.ask) return action.cmd;\n  const n = safeName(name);\n  return n ? action.cmd.replace(/\\{name\\}/g, n) : null;\n}\n\nexports._test = { actions, build, safeName };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const compose = () => String(ferrum.settings.get('dockerTools.composeCommand') || 'docker compose').trim().replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9 _.-]/g, '') || 'docker compose';\n\n  async function run(action) {\n    let name = '';\n    if (action.ask) {\n      name = (await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Name of the ' + action.ask, placeholder: 'For example: web, my-app:latest' })) || '';\n      if (!name.trim()) return;\n    }\n    const cmd = build(action, name);\n    if (!cmd) return ferrum.window.showMessage('That name has characters Docker names do not use. Use letters, digits and . _ - : / @ only.', 'warn');\n    if (action.confirm && !(await ferrum.window.confirm(action.confirm.replace('{name}', name.trim()) + '\\n\\n' + cmd, 'Run it'))) return;\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n  }\n\n  for (const a of actions('docker compose')) {\n    context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register('dockerTools.' + a.id, () => run(actions(compose()).find((x) => x.id === a.id))));\n  }\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('dockerTools.menu', async () => {\n      const list = actions(compose());\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(list.map((a) => ({ label: a.title, detail: a.cmd.replace('{name}', '<name>'), id: a.id })), { placeholder: 'Docker' });\n      if (pick) await run(list.find((a) => a.id === pick.id));\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('dockerTools.dockerfileBuild', async () => {\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n      const file = doc && doc.path && /(^|[\\\\/])(Dockerfile[\\w.-]*|[\\w.-]*\\.dockerfile)$/i.test(doc.path) ? doc.path : null;\n      if (!file) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a Dockerfile first.', 'warn');\n      const tag = ((await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Tag for the image', value: 'app:dev' })) || '').trim();\n      if (!safeName(tag)) return;\n      if (/[\"\\n\\r$`]/.test(file)) return ferrum.window.showMessage('The path of this file has characters I will not put in a command.', 'warn');\n      await ferrum.terminal.run('docker build -t ' + tag + ' -f \"' + file + '\" .');\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Docker Tools\n\nAbout 30 Docker and Compose commands in the palette, or in one menu (**Docker Menu...**): list containers, images, volumes and networks; follow logs; open a shell in a container; start, stop, restart and remove; pull, build and run an image; and for Compose: up, up with rebuild, down, stop, restart, ps, logs, exec, build, pull and config.\n\nEvery command is **typed in the terminal** where you see it run. Commands that delete things (**remove a container**, **prune**, **down with volumes**) show the exact command and ask first. Names you type are checked, so a stray space or `;` cannot turn into a second command.\n\n**Build the Open Dockerfile...** builds the Dockerfile you have open with a tag you choose.\n\nSet `dockerTools.composeCommand` to `docker-compose` if you still use Compose v1.\n\n## Permissions\n\n**terminal**, to type the commands. It does not read the terminal output or any file.\n"}}}